    "title": "Credential file read by a spawned program",
    "desc": "A program read a credential directly: private SSH keys, the shadow file, a git credential store, cloud or token files. Either a known reader (cat/less/base64/...) with the path on its command line, OR -- binary-agnostic -- any process whose file access (auditd PATH) touched one of these paths, which catches readers the command-line form misses (dd, cp, an interpreter, an editor). Routine accessors (passwd, sshd, PAM) are allow-listed.",
